# PHI / secrets — MUST never be committed.
# reports/ holds failed-coercion output which may contain raw cell values (PHI).
reports/
# data/ holds raw CMD batch report CSV pulls (patient-level PHI). Never commit.
data/
# Local CMD report CSV pulls feeding the Collections Explorer seed/cron — patient-level
# PHI (Patient Full Name / Member ID / Group Number). Read by cmdExplorerSeed.ts via
# CMD_EXPLORER_SEED_DIR. NEVER commit the data. *.csv is a blanket guard for the same
# reason (every CSV in this repo is a CMD PHI export); use `git add -f` for a rare
# deliberately-non-PHI csv.
Derek Historical Report Data/
Indigo Cron Job/
# Indigo Seed Data/ holds REAL Indigo patient PHI (CMD batch-dump CSV export). Load into
# Supabase staging.* only — NEVER commit. Its CSVs are already caught by *.csv below; this
# explicit folder entry guards any non-CSV file dropped there (mirrors the two folders above).
Indigo Seed Data/
*.csv
# ONE narrow exception to the blanket *.csv PHI guard above: the Kipu billing-report
# fixtures, which the hermetic suite needs. They are DERIVED and verified PHI-free —
# names/providers/auth numbers replaced and every date shifted -364 days (see that
# directory's README.md, and re-verify with a leak check before adding another).
# Keep this exception directory-scoped. NEVER broaden it, and never place a raw
# export here: real Kipu exports stay outside the repo.
#
# ⚠ PREFIX-SCOPED ON PURPOSE (tightened 2026-08-24). This directory is precisely where
# someone would drop a real export by mistake, and it was the ONE path the blanket *.csv
# guard above did not cover. Every scrubbed file carries the `fixture-` prefix, so
# narrowing the negation costs nothing and makes an accidental real export fall back
# under the blanket guard instead of becoming committable. NEVER widen this back to
# `*.csv`, and never rename a real export to `fixture-*`.
!test/fixtures/kipu-billing-report/fixture-*.csv
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

